# search-starter — environment contract
#
# A standalone Next.js search site (finder + live corpus graph + map + canonical
# PortableDoc reader) over ANY Barkpark dataset. Copy to `.env.local` for local
# dev; on the managed deploy path the site-deploy engine injects the BARKPARK_*
# vars at slot boot (deploy/lib/site-deploy-common.sh RUNTIME_ALLOW).
#
# The NAMES are identical across every adapter (next-starter, astro-starter,
# templates/DEPLOYING.md) so one .env works everywhere.

# ── Content link (required) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API base — a BARE origin (the finder's graph rides the flat /v1/graph route,
# which resolves the token's Default workspace; the seed corpus must live there,
# charter D13). Server-consumed only — NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_, never reaches the browser.
BARKPARK_API_URL=https://guerrilla.barkpark.cloud

# Server-only read token. A public dataset reads anonymously (leave unset). When
# set it must NEVER be NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed — Next would inline it into the client
# bundle. A read token additionally unlocks the token-scoped (Indx) search route.
BARKPARK_TOKEN=

# Dataset + tenancy the finder / reader / graph read from.
BARKPARK_DATASET=production
BARKPARK_WORKSPACE=default
BARKPARK_PROJECT=default

# ── Content types the finder surfaces + facets over ────────────────────────
# On the managed deploy path (the build env is scrubbed to BUILD_ALLOW) the
# server reads the singular BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE. For a Vercel / self-managed build,
# set the browser-visible list instead (comma-separated `type` or `type:Label`):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BARKPARK_DOC_TYPES=guide:Guides,ref:References
# Unset → the multi-type demo default (post,paper,sheet,page,author,category,project).
BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BARKPARK_DOC_TYPES=

# ── Live keystroke search — DERIVED, do not set by hand ────────────────────
# Per-keystroke search flips a single frame on ONE persistent WebSocket
# (browser → Phoenix Channel → engine), bypassing the HTTP /api/find proxy.
# It needs THREE browser-visible values, and next.config.mjs derives ALL THREE
# from the server vars above at build time — there is nothing to set here:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BARKPARK_WS_URL       = <origin of BARKPARK_API_URL>/socket
#                                       (origin STRIPS any /w/:ws/p/:proj suffix)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BARKPARK_WS_TOKEN     = BARKPARK_TOKEN
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BARKPARK_DATASET      = BARKPARK_DATASET   ← the silent one
#   (+ NEXT_PUBLIC_BARKPARK_WORKSPACE / _PROJECT, for portability)
#
# THE DATASET IS NOT OPTIONAL. The channel topic is
# `search:<workspace>:<project>:<dataset>`. A browser that never receives the
# dataset falls back to the "docs" default and asks for
# search:default:default:docs — a topic the server REFUSES when no such dataset
# exists in that project, replying to the join with reason "unknown_dataset".
# So the LIVE badge never lights and every keystroke keeps riding the
# same-origin HTTP route: search still WORKS, it just pays a round trip it did
# not have to. The refusal reason is in the browser console and the API log —
# that string is the whole diagnosis. If you ever hand-wire these three, wire
# all three.
#
# The token reaches the browser by design: it must be public-read only, granting
# nothing beyond the published reads this site already serves anonymously.
# BARKPARK_TOKEN empty → live search ships DARK (no socket at all) and every
# keystroke rides the same-origin HTTP path. No crash, no error state.

# ── Landing switch (LOCAL DEV ONLY) ────────────────────────────────────────
# "graph" (default) → the interactive corpus graph.
# NOTE: a managed deploy cannot set this. The control plane builds the deploy
# env as a fixed key map and the API rejects any BARKPARK_* name outside its
# allowlist, so no NEXT_PUBLIC_* name reaches a managed slot. Setting this is
# meaningful only when you run the site yourself.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FINDER_LANDING=graph

# ── Frontpage hero copy (brand it without touching code) ───────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_EYEBROW=Search
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_TITLE=Search everything.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_TAGLINE=Instant search across every document — misspellings widened server-side by Postgres trigram — with a live graph of how it all connects.

# ── Sub-path hosting + HEALTH markers (the deploy engine sets these) ────────
# The `/sites/<slug>/` path this site is served under. next.config.mjs bakes it
# as basePath + assetPrefix (the finder is multi-route, charter D6). Leave "/" for
# local dev at the domain root.
BARKPARK_SITE_BASE=/sites/search-starter/
# Deploy markers baked into the served HTML (<meta name="bp-build-id|bp-content-rev">)
# — the engine injects these at slot boot; the HEALTH gate asserts them.
BARKPARK_BUILD_ID=
BARKPARK_CONTENT_REV=

# ── @barkpark/react local override (TEMPORARY) ─────────────────────────────
# The published `@barkpark/react@1.0.0-preview.1` on npm contains NO PortableDoc,
# and the built PortableDoc renderer needs an `imageUrl` export the published
# `@barkpark/core@1.0.0-preview.3` does not yet carry (the changeset backlog is
# unpublished). Until the wave-1 human dispatch publishes the previews (task
# stw1-react-preview-publish), package.json pins BOTH to local `npm pack`s of the
# workspace's built dist:
#   "@barkpark/core":  "file:./vendor/barkpark-core.tgz"   (workspace preview.3, +imageUrl)
#   "@barkpark/react": "file:./vendor/barkpark-react.tgz"  (PortableDoc + paper-surface.css)
# ONCE the previews are live on npm: flip these to
#   "@barkpark/core":  "1.0.0-preview.3"   (or newer)
#   "@barkpark/react": "1.0.0-preview.2"
# and delete `vendor/`.

# ── Deploy-pinned theme (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# One of the shipped palettes: evergreen | ember | fjord | charple. Baked at
# BUILD as the data-bp-theme default (a visitor's own picker choice still wins).
# The deploy engine passes this from the request env (allow-listed, W2).
# BARKPARK_THEME=ember
